From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 17:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] inputMethod: A key the input method cannot answer for still
 reaches the window

Every key goes to the input method first and is given to the window only
when ibus has answered, even with a plain keyboard layout and no input
method in use. Switching windows re-targets ibus -- a focus out, a focus
in, a content type, and on a per-window input source a set-engine, which
is where "Set global engine failed: Operation was cancelled" in the
journal comes from -- and a key caught in that had nowhere to go: the
reply came back for a context that is no longer the current one, or with
an error, and the key was quietly dropped. The person saw the first
letters of what they typed disappear.

A key the input method does not answer for now goes to the window
unfiltered, which is what would have happened had ibus said it did not
want it.
diff --git a/js/misc/inputMethod.js b/js/misc/inputMethod.js
index 4d123c3..3c0ec11 100644
--- a/js/misc/inputMethod.js
+++ b/js/misc/inputMethod.js
@@ -346,8 +346,17 @@ export const InputMethod = GObject.registerClass({
             event.get_key_code() - 8, // Convert XKB keycodes to evcodes
             state, -1, this._cancellable,
             (context, res) => {
-                if (context !== this._context)
+                // The key was taken from the window while the input method
+                // looked at it, so it has to come back one way or another:
+                // if the input method did not take it, or could not answer
+                // because it was re-targeted or went away, the key is still
+                // the person's and goes to the window unfiltered. Switching
+                // windows re-targets the input method, and a key swallowed
+                // there is a letter the person watched disappear.
+                if (context !== this._context) {
+                    this.notify_key_event(event, false);
                     return;
+                }
 
                 try {
                     const retval = context.process_key_event_async_finish(res);
@@ -355,6 +364,7 @@ export const InputMethod = GObject.registerClass({
                 } catch (e) {
                     if (!e.matches(Gio.IOErrorEnum, Gio.IOErrorEnum.CANCELLED))
                         log(`Error processing key on IM: ${e.message}`);
+                    this.notify_key_event(event, false);
                 }
             });
         return true;
